      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SECTION A: TIME, SPEED & DISTANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Time, Speed & Distance covers core principles including speed conversion, relative speed, average speed, and train-based problems.",
        "Basic Mensuration is divided into two dimensions (2D plane figures) and three dimensions (3D solid figures).",
        "Data Interpretation tests the ability to extract, analyze, and compute quantitative information from structured datasets.",
        "Solving practice questions along with verifying against the answer key builds accuracy and time management for competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "i50b919"
    },
    {
      "id": "5tuxift",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. BASIC CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h9tj9mj",
      "content": "Speed = Distance / Time<br></br>Distance = Speed × Time<br></br>Time = Distance / Speed<br></br><br></br>SSC questions from this area are direct and calculation-light."
    },
    {
      "id": "qguh6ud",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. SPEED CONVERSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gdpic00",
      "content": "1 km/hr = 5/18 m/s<br></br>1 m/s = 18/5 km/hr<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>36 km/hr = 36 × 5/18 = 10 m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "u3rz0eq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. AVERAGE SPEED"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sd2sf76",
      "content": "For equal distance:<br></br>Average speed = (2xy)/(x+y)<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>40 km/hr and 60 km/hr<br></br>Average speed = 48 km/hr"
    },
    {
      "id": "46cskw5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4. RELATIVE SPEED"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b45ffl1",
      "content": "Same direction: Difference of speeds<br></br>Opposite direction: Sum of speeds<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>50 km/hr and 70 km/hr (opposite)<br></br>Relative speed = 120 km/hr"
    },
    {
      "id": "5xhsrji",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5. TRAIN PROBLEMS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pdl4z9w",
      "content": "Time to cross an object = Length / Relative speed<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>Train length = 100 m, time = 10 s<br></br>Speed = 10 m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "hqhgv7w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SECTION B: BASIC MENSURATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cmlzms8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6. 2D FIGURES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7oap31y",
      "content": "Square:<br></br>Area = a², Perimeter = 4a<br></br><br></br>Rectangle:<br></br>Area = l × b, Perimeter = 2(l+b)<br></br><br></br>Circle:<br></br>Area = πr², Circumference = 2πr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6e53nmn",
      "content": "Example:<br></br>Radius = 7 cm<br></br>Area = 154 cm²"
    },
    {
